[[build-errors]]
=== Error propagation

**STUB**: Specifies how a failure travels through a program. Covers a foreign
exception in one pool, a runtime fault such as a failed allocation, and a
crashed process. Each becomes an error packet, crosses process boundaries with
its context intact, and reaches the caller, either as a `Try` value or as the
CLI's error output and exit code. Defines what information is preserved at each
hop.

